<metadata><name>Mount Bailey and Hemlock Butte</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:307-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.107545" lon="-122.185306"><ele>1648.9</ele><name>Three Lakes Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:three-lakes-sno-park (OSM way 614077864); confidence: high; pdf_page: 308; book_elev_ft: 5400; quote: map 74: THREE LAKES SNO-PARK 5400'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.124009" lon="-122.165836"><ele>1594.1</ele><name>Silent Creek Trail / Mount Bailey Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM node shared by Mount Bailey Trail (way 180777157), Mt Bailey Nordic and Bailey Road; confidence: high; pdf_page: 309; quote: At 1.5 miles pass the Mount Bailey Trail junction</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.135846" lon="-122.196593"><ele>1847.5</ele><name>Road 380 junction north of Hemlock Butte</name><desc>source: OSM node shared by Mount Bailey Trail and Hemlock Butte Road (road 380); the ski cabin (OSM node 2123311719) is 400 m SE; confidence: high; pdf_page: 309; quote: around the north side of Hemlock Butte to open areas for views. This is near where an old forest road, 380, intersects the trail.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.155101" lon="-122.220014"><ele>2551.1</ele><name>Mount Bailey summit</name><desc>source: OSM peak node 357324366 = end of Mount Bailey Trail way 1187977255; confidence: high; pdf_page: 309; book_elev_ft: 8363; quote: Continue steeply up the narrowing ridge to the summit</desc></wpt>
